        "Juan Ignacio Cirac",
        "Peter Zoller",
        "Rainer Blatt"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Trapped ions established a powerful route to controlled quantum dynamics and entanglement, turning quantum information proposals into precise laboratory physics.",
        "attribution": "Cirac and Zoller supplied foundational theoretical proposals, while Blatt's experiments demonstrated and extended the control of trapped-ion systems.",
        "maturity": "The central techniques have been reproduced, improved, and used to demonstrate increasingly capable quantum operations and simulations.",
        "uncertainties": [
